  "statement": "# Bush 522 — task brief\n\nThis is a design target, not an implementation specification. Build your own GDD, scene structure, rules, and code.\n\n## Target player experience\n\nFly a light bush plane off a home runway, manage throttle and attitude across open procedural terrain, set it down beside a distant checkpoint, and bring it home for a deliberate finish.\n\n## Scope boundary\n\nOne continuous flight course with real flight physics, a fuel and score readout, a qualifying outbound landing, a return leg, a home landing, and separate victory and crash endings.\n\n## Creative freedom\n\nYou may choose terrain dressing, instrument layout, camera framing, and audio while preserving player-controlled flight, the out-and-back objective order, and both terminal states.\n"
